==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|recapitulatus}}, past participle of {{term|recapitulare||to go over the main points of a thing again}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|re-||again|lang=la}} + {{term|capitulum||a head, main part, chapter}}; see [[capitulate]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Canada|UK}} {{IPA|/riːkəˈpɪtʃʊleɪt/|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|recapitulat}}

# to [[summarize]] or repeat in concise form
#: ''The entire [[symphony]] was '''recapitulated''' in the last four [[bars]].''
# to repeat the evolutionary stages of an organism during its embryonic development
#: ''[[ontogeny|Ontogeny]] '''recapitulates''' [[phylogeny]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to summarize or repeat in concise form}} [[recap]], [[sum up]]

